# Security-scan suppressions for false positives, file-specific.
# Each suppression has a preceding `# why:` line documenting the audit.
# To re-audit, run the security scan and compare the new findings against
# this list — only specific files appearing in the prior 1012-finding run
# are listed here.

# why: pnpm lockfile contains base64-encoded SHA256 integrity hashes for
# every package version (the `integrity:` field). detect-secrets flags
# these as high-entropy strings but they are content checksums, not
# credentials. 996/1012 findings in the prior scan came from this file.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# why: detect-secrets flagged 4 lines in the upstream .gitignore as
# high-entropy. Inspecting the file, those lines are common ignore patterns
# (e.g. `*.tsbuildinfo`, lockfile globs); no credentials. Upstream artifact,
# not authored by this fork.
.gitignore

# why: contains illustrative env-var values like `OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxx`,
# `MILVUS_TOKEN=your-token` for users to replace. detect-secrets cannot
# distinguish placeholder strings from real keys; the user-replacement
# pattern is established convention for tutorial docs.
README.md

# why: same placeholder-env-var pattern as README.md; quick-start guide
# tells users how to set their own keys, not real keys.
docs/getting-started/quick-start.md

# why: MCP package README documents `OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxx` placeholder
